The code in src/, include/, cli/, tests/, and tools/ is an independent
implementation written in modern C++20. It builds on published and
public-domain algorithmic techniques:
  - LZ77 with recent-offset reuse and split token streams (Flash, Beam, Prism)
  - Burrows-Wheeler / move-to-front block sorting and context mixing (Crystal, Prism)
  - Asymmetric Numeral Systems (rANS / tANS, published into the public domain
    by Jarek Duda)
  - 12-state LZMA markov automaton, distance slot modeling, adaptive binary
    range coding, and x86/ARM64 BCJ branch target normalization (originating
    in the public-domain LZMA SDK by Igor Pavlov and 0BSD/public-domain
    XZ Utils / liblzma by Lasse Collin; re-architected in Laser with a 5-stream
    decoupled range decoder and nibble-split literal model)
  - Fast 64-bit content hashing inspired by xxHashprime constants (Yann Collet)

No third-party source code has been copied into src/, include/, cli/ or tests/.

